      "scientificName": "Stylurus scudderi",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/91006967/medium.jpeg",
      "distinction": "Among its hanging clubtail relatives, the zebra clubtail stands out with its bold, high-contrast striped pattern - the arrow clubtail has more muted markings with arrow-like shapes rather than stripes, while the riverine clubtail shows more olive-brown coloration with less distinct banding."
    }
